# Protection's prevention and Ancient Adamantoise's redirection both want to change the 2 damage Pyroclasm would deal to
# Bot1's Llanowar Elves, which Mother of Runes has given protection from red: the Elves' controller chooses which applies
# first (CR 616.1). Bot1 has the damage prevented, and then there is no damage left to redirect (CR 615.1). The 2 damage
# to Mother of Runes is dealt to the Adamantoise instead, and the Adamantoise takes its own 2: 4 in all, and every
# creature lives. The other order is ancient-adamantoise-pyroclasm-on-a-protected-elf-its-controller-redirects-it-first.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Ancient Adamantoise
Forest
Mox Pearl
Mother of Runes
Llanowar Elves
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Pyroclasm
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ancient Adamantoise)
Bot2.Choose()
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Pyroclasm.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Activate(Llanowar Elves)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Colors(Red)
Bot1.Replace(protection)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Battlefield.Ancient Adamantoise.Damage = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Damage = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Damage = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Pyroclasm
